Description: Makefile: link the libraries V\OS ships
 Upstream lists "network be tracker translation textencoding columnlistview"
 in LIBS. V\OS ships no -lnetwork and no -lcolumnlistview: the legacy
 endpoint network library was dropped in favour of POSIX sockets (the app is
 built with BONE_BUILD and already uses socket()/recv() from libc), and
 BColumnListView/BColumn live in libbe on V\OS (src/kits/interface/
 ColumnListView.cpp is part of the interface kit), so those symbols resolve
 through -lbe. What stays: be, tracker, translation, textencoding --
 libnetwork's absence, libcolumnlistview's absence and the presence of the
 other three were checked against the installed vos/vos-dev packages.
 -lroot is exported by the vos_makefile_engine buildsystem class;
 STDCPPLIBS was already listed by upstream.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: vendor
Last-Update: 2026-10-23
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
 #	- 	if your library does not follow the standard library naming scheme,
 #		you need to specify the path to the library and it's name.
 #		(e.g. for mylib.a, specify "mylib.a" or "path/mylib.a")
-LIBS = network be tracker translation textencoding columnlistview $(STDCPPLIBS)
+LIBS = be tracker translation textencoding $(STDCPPLIBS)
 
 #	Specify additional paths to directories following the standard libXXX.so
 #	or libXXX.a naming scheme. You can specify full paths or paths relative
